Chapter 11
Activity: the Turnovers
النشاط: معدلات الدوران
Liquidity ratios say what a company holds. Leverage and coverage say how it is financed and whether it can carry the charge. Neither says anything about speed, and speed is where most working capital is lost.
A turnover ratio divides a flow by the balance that produced it, and the answer is a number of times a year. Receivables that turn over ten times a year are collected in about five weeks; receivables that turn over four times a year are collected in about three months, and the company has financed the difference. The Learning Outcome Statements name five turnovers, and this chapter computes all of them.
Figure F511-01 is your map.
Figure F511-01. Chapter 11 roadmap: five balances, five flows, five speeds.
