@table
Item | Amount
Net sales | 21,978,000
Cost of goods sold | 18,900,000
Average accounts receivable | 1,830,000
Average inventory | 2,100,000
Average accounts payable | 1,400,000
Purchases (inventory rose 280,000) | 19,180,000
Accounts receivable turnover | ________
Inventory turnover | ________
Accounts payable turnover | ________
@end
LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Turnover" has two meanings
In American English and on the CMA exam, turnover means the number of times a balance is replaced in a year. In British English, turnover also means revenue: a company's annual turnover is its sales. Arabic معدل الدوران is the first sense and إيرادات the second; French rotation and chiffre d'affaires likewise. The exam always means the first.
